{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["<b>But on the fifteenth day, you shall celebrate.</b> A shelamim offering for the festival sacrifice — one might think it can override Shabbat; therefore Scripture says אַךְ — since it has make-up days all seven." "<b>When you gather in the produce of the land.</b> That this seventh month should come at the time of gathering. From here they were commanded to intercalate the years — for if not for intercalation, sometimes it would fall in the middle of summer or winter." "<b>You shall celebrate.</b> Shelamim of the festival sacrifice." "<b>Seven days.</b> If he did not bring on this one, he may bring on another — one might think he may bring them all seven; therefore Scripture says <b>and you shall celebrate it</b> — one day is meant, and not more. Then why are seven stated? For make-up days (Ḥagigah 9)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:03.109192956Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}